First of all, I would like to say 'HI' to everyone, for it has been a long time
since I have posted.  I used to do it a good deal, but now I am on summer
break, and when I do come to the school, I play nethack (but it isn't working 
now, so I read the news.

Spoilers follow






Anyway, there are MANY nice things to wish for, and wishing for something that
you might be able to get otherwise is not always bad.  But for myself, I   
always play a priest, and I wish for a blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir.
After that comes grey(or gray, I can never remember) dragon scale mail (magic
resistance, you know).  Then boots of speed, or gauntlets of power, or other
high power armour.  Now, if you are into the more unusual wishes, get 3 cursed
scrolls of genocide...Sounds strange, but what, on higher levels, do you want
to meet at least 10 or 15 of?  Or 2 or 3 blessed luckstones.  If you want the
express trip to the wizard, get a cursed scroll of teleportation.  BUT FIRST,
ABOVE ALL, get a blessed scroll (actually, get 3) of charging.  You can only
recharge the wand once, but you can use them on other things.  Also, 
perchance you may want 3 blessed spellbooks of identify.  As you can see,
there are many good choices, so try several and have fun.
>2. Also in two games I wished for "a blessed +3 broadsword named
>Stormbringer" and in one I got it & in another I just got a blessed +0
>broadsword named Stormbringer (still a great weapon). I of course got
>this information after my demise.

Well, as I understand it, the problem is in your luck.  What you need to get
first are 2 or 3 blessed luckstones, let your luck go up, and then wish for the
sword.

>3. Will #dipping stuff in holy water merely bless it (from cursed to
>uncursed) or will it enchant it as well.

It will go from cursed to uncursed and uncursed to blessed, but it does NOT
charge things.

>4. Is there any point (as a barbarian) in my #naming my two handed
>sword Orcrist (say after Morrigan blesses it in a prayer or even
>before that)?

I have no idea, but you do have two #4s.

>4. What do you use a scroll of charging for - only on wands/magic
>markers/magic lamps or will they work on weapons?

No, they do not work on weapons, thus the famous 'you have a feeling of loss'.

>5. How do you convert "bad" potions to water/ holy water.

Well, drop them on the holiest altar(this is too easy, I am not going to spell
it out)

